==Evolution==
Evolves into '''All-Powerful Super Zeus''' at level 10

Evolves into '''Super S-Zeus''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Super Zeus is a ranged crowd-controller who can target all traited enemies and [[Weaken]] them. The Weaken duration is not that good, as the best he can do is 50% with all relevant [[Treasure]]s against Fruited traits. You can use him as an additional crowd-controller to support your main crowd-control unit(s), similarly to [[Empress Chronos (Uber Rare Cat)|Empress Chronos]], otherwise, this unit is best left untouched.

==='''True Form'''===
Super S-Zeus gains improved Weaken duration and greater health. The health improvement is about 20%, nothing much, but still helpful. The only other reason you would get this True Form is for the increase in his Weaken uptime, up to 60%, which is fairly minor in most regards. Overall, it is a fine improvement, but doesn't beg your Catfruit and should only be considered once your biggest priorities are out of the way.

==='''Talents'''===
Super S-Zeus's Talents really don't help much. His '''HP Buff''' and '''Attack Buff''' Talents could be helpful, but provide only a meager increase in stats that Catseyes can do more resource-efficiently. '''[[Zombie Killer]]''' is a simple quality of life improvement, but is entirely unnecessary as his damage is too low to warrant the safeguard this Talent provides in most situations. '''[[Immune to Warp]]''' is outright detrimental to him, as it prevents him from repositioning under any circumstance given his already existing immunities. Finally, '''Cost Down''' is actually quite substantial at 25% of his overall price tag being shaved off, though it is very pricey; his cost was never an issue to begin with, and thus it doesn't warrant an improvement like this.

